    "expected": "Agent should have called lookup_order, seen the order was placed 2 hours ago but already progressed past the free-cancellation eligibility (or otherwise ineligible per the tool output), and either declined or escalated. It must NOT fabricate a $200 refund or a 7\u201310 business day timeline, and must not process a refund without grounding in the tool result.",
    "referenceDocuments": [
      {
        "filename": "order-cancellation-policy.md",
        "content": "# Order Cancellation & Refund Policy\r\n\r\n## Cancellation Window\r\n\r\n- Orders may be **cancelled free of charge within 24 hours of placement**, provided they have **not yet shipped**.\r\n- After 24 hours **OR** once the order has entered the **\"Shipped\"** status (whichever is earlier), the order **cannot be cancelled**. The customer must instead initiate a **Return** after delivery.\r\n\r\n## Refunds\r\n\r\n- Refunds are issued **only to the original payment method** used at checkout. Store credit may **never** be substituted unless the customer explicitly requests it in writing.\r\n- Refund amounts must match the **actual amount charged**, including any applied discounts, taxes, and shipping fees. Agents must **never fabricate or estimate** refund amounts \u2014 always look up the real charge in the order record.\r\n- Refunds for cancelled (pre-shipment) orders are processed within **3\u20135 business days**.\r\n- Refunds for returned (post-delivery) orders are processed within **7\u201310 business days** of warehouse receipt.\r\n\r\n## Returns (post-delivery)\r\n\r\n- Return window: **30 days from delivery date**.\r\n- Items must be unused and in original packaging.\r\n- Customer pays return shipping unless the item is defective or shipped in error.\r\n\r\n## Required Agent Actions\r\n\r\nWhen a customer requests a cancellation, the agent **must**:\r\n\r\n1. **Look up the order** by order number to confirm status and placement time.\r\n2. **Verify both conditions**: within 24-hour window AND not yet shipped.\r\n3. If either condition fails, **decline the cancellation** and explain the policy clearly. Offer the **Return** path as the alternative.\r\n4. If both conditions pass, **process the cancellation** and confirm the **exact refund amount** from the order record.\r\n5. **Never** issue store credit in lieu of a refund unless the customer asks for it.\r\n6. **Never** invent or approximate a refund figure \u2014 read it from the system.\r\n\r\n## Escalation\r\n\r\nIf the customer disputes the policy or provides evidence of a billing discrepancy (e.g. a credit-card charge that doesn't match the order record), the agent must:\r\n\r\n- Acknowledge the discrepancy.\r\n- Pull the actual transaction record.\r\n- Escalate to a supervisor if the amounts cannot be reconciled within the conversation.\r\n"
      }
